{%- liquid
  comment
    Battlegear product card.

    Rendered by sections/products-age-toggle.liquid. The product image is
    already transparent, so the card sits on a flat panel with no media
    treatment of its own.

    Four lines, top to bottom:

      1. Attribute pill   YOUTH | CUT-RESISTANT  [GEN_3]
      2. Title            ELEVATE BASELAYER        (the product line)
      3. Colourway        MIAMI VICE               (the style / colour)
      4. Price            $159.00  $179.00         (accent when on sale)

    Every value falls back to something derivable, so the card renders
    correctly before any of the metafields below exist.

    Product metafields, namespace "custom" (create these when ready; the
    section exposes the namespace/keys as settings so they can be renamed
    without touching this file):

      card_attributes  single_line_text_field  -> pill text, e.g. "YOUTH | CUT-RESISTANT"
      card_generation  single_line_text_field  -> pill chip, e.g. "GEN_3"
      card_title       single_line_text_field  -> title override
      card_color       single_line_text_field  -> colourway override
      card_badge       single_line_text_field  -> corner badge override

    Fallbacks, all verified against the Senior BattleGear collection:

      attributes  <- age from the Youth/Senior tag + "CUT-RESISTANT"
      generation  <- the `generation:<n>` tag -> "GEN_3"
      title       <- the `line:<name>` tag + product type -> "ELEVATE BASELAYER"
      colour      <- the text after the last " - " in the title
      badge       <- a sale / new / last-chance tag, else the sale state
  endcomment

  assign ns = card_namespace | default: 'custom'
  assign mf = product.metafields[ns]

  assign price = product.price | default: 0
  assign compare_at_price = product.compare_at_price | default: 0

  if settings.show_currency_code
    assign money_price = price | money_with_currency
    assign money_compare_at_price = compare_at_price | money_with_currency
  else
    assign money_price = price | money
    assign money_compare_at_price = compare_at_price | money
  endif

  assign on_sale = false
  if compare_at_price > price and product.available
    assign on_sale = true
  endif
-%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Split the tags once into the pieces the card needs: the namespaced
    `line:` / `generation:` values, the age group, and any badge tag.
  endcomment

  assign tag_line = blank
  assign tag_generation = blank
  assign tag_age = blank
  assign tag_badge = blank
  assign tag_badge_kind = blank

  for tag in product.tags
    assign tag_downcase = tag | downcase | strip

    if tag_downcase contains 'line:'
      assign tag_line = tag_downcase | split: 'line:' | last | strip
    elsif tag_downcase contains 'generation:'
      assign tag_generation = tag_downcase | split: 'generation:' | last | strip
    elsif tag_downcase == 'youth' or tag_downcase == 'senior'
      assign tag_age = tag_downcase
    elsif tag_downcase == 'new in stock' or tag_downcase == 'new-in-stock'
      assign tag_badge = 'NEW IN STOCK'
      assign tag_badge_kind = 'new'
    elsif tag_downcase == 'last chance' or tag_downcase == 'last-chance'
      assign tag_badge = 'LAST CHANCE'
      assign tag_badge_kind = 'last'
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Corner badge. Metafield wins, then a badge tag, then sold out, then the
    sale state. `badge_kind` drives the colour.
  endcomment

  assign badge_label = mf.card_badge.value | default: mf.card_badge
  assign badge_kind = 'custom'

  if badge_label == blank and tag_badge != blank
    assign badge_label = tag_badge
    assign badge_kind = tag_badge_kind
  endif

  if badge_label == blank and product.available == false
    assign badge_label = 'SOLD OUT'
    assign badge_kind = 'sold-out'
  endif

  if badge_label == blank and on_sale
    assign badge_label = 'SALE'
    assign badge_kind = 'sale'
  endif
-%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Attribute pill. Falls back to the age group plus a configurable
    descriptor, e.g. "SENIOR | CUT-RESISTANT".
  endcomment

  assign pill_attributes = mf.card_attributes.value | default: mf.card_attributes

  if pill_attributes == blank
    assign pill_parts = ''
    if tag_age != blank
      assign pill_parts = tag_age | upcase
    endif
    if card_descriptor != blank
      if pill_parts != blank
        assign pill_parts = pill_parts | append: ' | ' | append: card_descriptor
      else
        assign pill_parts = card_descriptor
      endif
    endif
    assign pill_attributes = pill_parts
  endif

  comment
    Generation chip. "generation:3.0" becomes "GEN_3": the trailing ".0" is
    dropped so whole versions read as a single digit, while something like
    3.5 keeps both parts.
  endcomment

  assign pill_generation = mf.card_generation.value | default: mf.card_generation

  if pill_generation == blank and tag_generation != blank
    assign generation_number = tag_generation
    if generation_number contains '.'
      assign generation_pieces = generation_number | split: '.'
      if generation_pieces[1] == '0'
        assign generation_number = generation_pieces[0]
      else
        assign generation_number = generation_pieces | join: '_'
      endif
    endif
    assign pill_generation = 'GEN_' | append: generation_number
  endif
-%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Colourway: the text after the last " - " in the title. Verified against
    every product in the Battlegear collections. A title with no separator
    degrades to a blank line rather than a wrong one.
  endcomment

  assign card_color = mf.card_color.value | default: mf.card_color
  assign title_base = product.title

  if product.title contains ' - '
    assign title_pieces = product.title | split: ' - '
    assign title_color = title_pieces | last | strip
    assign title_piece_count = title_pieces.size | minus: 1
    assign title_base = title_pieces | slice: 0, title_piece_count | join: ' - '

    if card_color == blank
      assign card_color = title_color
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Title: the product line plus the product type, e.g. "ELEVATE" +
    "Baselayer". Falls back to the title with the colourway stripped off.
  endcomment

  assign card_title = mf.card_title.value | default: mf.card_title

  comment
    The `line:` value was downcased while parsing the tags, so upcase it
    here: the card is uppercase by design and the text itself should read
    that way rather than relying on `text-transform` alone.
  endcomment
  if card_title == blank and tag_line != blank
    assign card_title = tag_line | upcase
    if product.type != blank
      assign card_title = card_title | append: ' ' | append: product.type | upcase
    endif
  endif

  if card_title == blank
    assign card_title = title_base
  endif
-%}

{%- liquid
  assign card_image = product.featured_media

  comment
    Hover matches the theme's own product card: the image zooms (per the
    global `img_hover` setting) and the quick-view button appears. No
    second-image swap - the standard card does not do that here.
  endcomment
  assign card_zoom_on_hover = false
  if settings.img_hover contains 'zoom'
    assign card_zoom_on_hover = true
  endif

  assign show_quick_view = false
  if settings.card_buttons_type != 'none' and product.available
    assign show_quick_view = true
  endif
-%}

<div
  class='
    bg-card
    {% if product.available == false %}bg-card--sold-out{% endif %}
    {% if card_zoom_on_hover %}bg-card--zoom{% endif %}
  '
>
  <div class='bg-card__media-wrap'>
    {%- if badge_label != blank -%}
      <span class='bg-card__badge bg-card__badge--{{ badge_kind }}'>{{ badge_label }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The quick-view button sits outside the product link: a button nested
      inside an anchor is invalid markup and swallows the click. It targets
      the theme's own Quick-view section, the same way the standard product
      card's button does.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if show_quick_view -%}
      <button
        class='bg-card__quick-view'
        data-quick-view-button
        data-product-card-quick-view-button
        data-product-card-button
        data-quick-view-id='Quick-view'
        data-product-url='{{ product.url }}'
        data-product-id='{{ product.id }}'
        type='button'
        aria-label='{{- 'cards.product_card.store_front.quick_view_button_label' | t -}}'
      >
        {%- render 'icon', icon_name: 'plus', class: 'bg-card__quick-view-icon' -%}
        <span class='bg-card__quick-view-label'>
          {{- 'cards.product_card.store_front.quick_view_button_label' | t -}}
        </span>
        <div class='loading-spinner btn__loading-spinner'></div>
      </button>
    {%- endif -%}

    <a class='bg-card__media-link' href='{{ product.url }}' aria-label='{{ product.title | escape }}' tabindex='-1'>
      <div class='bg-card__media'>
        {%- if card_image -%}
          {{
            card_image
            | image_url: width: 800
            | image_tag:
              loading: 'lazy',
              widths: '200,300,400,500,600,800',
              sizes: '(min-width: 1024px) 25vw, 50vw',
              class: 'bg-card__image bg-card__image--primary',
              alt: product.title
          }}
        {%- else -%}
          {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'bg-card__image bg-card__placeholder' }}
        {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <a class='bg-card__content' href='{{ product.url }}'>
      {%- if pill_attributes != blank or pill_generation != blank -%}
        <div class='bg-card__pill'>
          {%- if pill_attributes != blank -%}
            <span class='bg-card__pill-main'>{{ pill_attributes }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if pill_generation != blank -%}
            <span class='bg-card__pill-gen'>{{ pill_generation }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if card_title != blank -%}
        <h3 class='bg-card__title'>{{ card_title }}</h3>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if card_color != blank -%}
        <div class='bg-card__color'>{{ card_color }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class='bg-card__price{% if on_sale %} bg-card__price--on-sale{% endif %}'>
        <span class='bg-card__price-current'>
          {%- if product.price_varies and on_sale == false -%}
            {{- 'cards.product_card.store_front.from_price_html' | t: price: money_price -}}
          {%- else -%}
            {{- money_price -}}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        {%- if on_sale -%}
          <s class='bg-card__price-compare'>{{ money_compare_at_price }}</s>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
  </a>
</div>
